# Experiment output hygiene

- Apply this rule to the entire LoopJev project.
- Keep logs/ for concise run logs only; do not store tensor caches, checkpoints, reports, or script backups there.
- Keep reusable features and model state under artifacts/<experiment>/cache/ and artifacts/<experiment>/results/.
- Use work/ or the system temporary directory for intermediate scripts, downloads, and checks.
- After verifying the replacement run, promptly remove agent-created failed runs, small debugging pilots, redundant caches, and obsolete script backups.
- Keep only the active reproducible experiment, essential metrics, predictions, and configuration unless the user asks to retain alternatives.
- Before deleting outputs, inspect exact paths and identify ownership; do not delete user data, model weights, source code, or active experiment results.
- Avoid broad deletion globs and do not create new backup copies on every edit.
- Reuse cached frozen features for additional readouts; recompute after backbone or prompt changes.
- Report cleanup briefly and do not start unrelated experiments while explaining existing results.
